Basque does seem to be a isolate, but there are proposed links to
Caucasian languages [the region, not the ethnic group].

Etruscan was the language isolate you were thinking of, but a quick
google search seems to indicate that Etruscan isn't understood enough to
link it to any language.

Burushaski (spoken in northern Kashmir) seems to be unrelated to any
known language.

Ainu, spoken in the northern Japanese isles, is also a language isolate.

Japanese (and to a slightly lesser extent, Korean) are also considered
language isolates by many.  [Found an interesting theory that suggested
that Japanese was related to the Dravidian language group of southern
India!]

As usual, wikipedia has a decent article on ``language isolates.''

